adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";N;s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:130905;s:5:\"title\";s:19:\"The Charcoal People\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"pt\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:13:\"Os Carvoeiros\";s:8:\"overview\";s:435:\"This deeply human documentary examines the subject of environmental destruction, highlighting the impoverished migrant workers who are chopping down the Amazon rainforest to create charcoal for pig iron production used primarily in the automobile industry. The film examines the children and elders and their daily lives and work as they burn timber in igloo-looking huts, their bodies charred gray for $2 a day, struggling to survive.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:2.9454;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/oAwC2z0VddnNash6NZItpxO8Uz5.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2000-01-20\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:8;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:7;}i:2;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/qT2ZAUhwWHUf4ZbaBPsLbEpG5q9.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:1722166;s:5:\"title\";s:39:\"Tagliamento - King of The Alpine Rivers\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"de\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:39:\"Tagliamento – König der Alpenflüsse\";s:8:\"overview\";s:601:\"The Tagliamento, known as the \"King of the Alpine Rivers,\" is considered Europe\'s last untamed river. Its course stretches from the peaks of the Dolomites to the Adriatic coast. With its braided riverbed, crystal-clear waters, and untouched banks, it shapes one of Europe\'s most remarkable natural landscapes. Wildcats and golden jackals roam the forests along its shores, while the river also flows through the Laguna di Marano, a rich brackish lagoon inhabited by swans and flamingos. Its journey ends at the Adriatic Sea, where the Tagliamento has been shaping the coastline for thousands of years.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:2.8163;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/5ThdjPozaIpMotFx4velR7olZaB.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2024-11-12\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:0;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:0;}i:3;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/hAlB9MaamrP1eDhGA4AkjSAPxAf.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:501;s:5:\"title\";s:11:\"Grizzly Man\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:11:\"Grizzly Man\";s:8:\"overview\";s:271:\"Follows the story of \"Grizzly Man\" Timothy Treadwell and what the thirteen summers in a National Park in Alaska were like in his attempt to protect the grizzly bears. The film is full of unique images and a look into the spirit of a man who sacrificed himself for nature.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.8144;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/zuZWpcuye25rpsiZ4XzsAvmLDHG.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2005-08-12\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:7.531;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:962;}i:4;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";N;s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:1722205;s:5:\"title\";s:9:\"Unnatural\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"fr\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:13:\"Contre nature\";s:8:\"overview\";s:416:\"In this era of profound ecosystem devastation and capitalist ravage, how is it that queer people are still the ones we deem “unnatural”? The director of this short film sought the help of their own community of rural queerdos, to tackle the big questions of our time. How are capitalism and sciences linked? Is heterosexuality natural or artificial? Is this chair straight or gay? Is this party starting or what?\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.92;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/ciDRuBbSPamPUOZ96sGCfwyRQOW.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:0;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:0;}i:5;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/uWenoHJWroFg7knGte2zm6LCzO4.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:2:{i:0;i:16;i:1;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:1593482;s:5:\"title\";s:15:\"Venezia Diorama\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:15:\"Venezia Diorama\";s:8:\"overview\";s:385:\"Through a series of animated art boards depicting a decaying Venice, the film unfolds like a set of postcards, capturing the mythical city\'s final moments of fragility.  Blending archival footage with contemporary observations, and anchored by the story of the 1902 collapse of St Mark\'s Campanile, Venezia Diorama invites us to reflect on a city slowly eroding, yet suspended in time.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.8511;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/gefvwhOGXygCIPRwvY0IYyWV6IG.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2026-01-31\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:0;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:0;}i:6;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/AcvxSLa140z7qgGQ8G2UjhcgVEY.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:2:{i:0;i:99;i:1;i:80;}s:2:\"id\";i:801058;s:5:\"title\";s:10:\"Seaspiracy\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:10:\"Seaspiracy\";s:8:\"overview\";s:151:\"Passionate about ocean life, a filmmaker sets out to document the harm that humans do to marine species — and uncovers an alarming global conspiracy.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.6576;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/iFNri0fwn1WfCoxf3H3v1z8dCm4.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2021-03-24\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:7.808;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:462;}i:7;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/ao8eOWxEf2Cecn7EtQrN8lhdDs3.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:1510913;s:5:\"title\";s:13:\"Soulèvements\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"fr\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:13:\"Soulèvements\";s:8:\"overview\";s:639:\"A choral portrait with 16 voices, 16 unique trajectories, reflective and intimate, of an intergenerational resistance movement led by young people who live and fight against land and water grabbing, industrial devastation, the rise of totalitarianism, and face political repression. A deep dive into the heart of Soulèvements de la Terre, revealing the unprecedented composition of the multiple forces deployed throughout the country, experimenting with other ways of life, forging new links with living things, thus overturning the established divisions between the political and the sensitive, opening us up to a field of possibilities.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.9628;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/4BdPMaFr3YCkXo7ykCIkbDEoMYO.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2026-02-11\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:8.3;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:3;}i:8;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/mGBmiWmi7JqeTWnrPicRbkXcsuO.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:410718;s:5:\"title\";s:16:\"Before the Flood\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:16:\"Before the Flood\";s:8:\"overview\";s:175:\"A look at how climate change affects our environment and what society can do to prevent the demise of endangered species, ecosystems, and native communities across the planet.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.5981;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/2fFTLaLbm8Ak7JBSYQ8Mb3jcFx9.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2016-10-21\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:7.7;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:821;}i:9;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/vdalavw8Z3t19hh6cQAUNhmxmKr.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:1603020;s:5:\"title\";s:27:\"Le grand cirque des marées\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"fr\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:27:\"Le grand cirque des marées\";s:8:\"overview\";s:233:\"The foreshore as you\'ve never seen it before! War, survival, and marine ballet: in a Microscomos-style odyssey with sumptuous images, this documentary takes a close-up look at the aquatic world at low tide and its colorful creatures.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.4191;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/j5i3enEg79hrbHnp5fQS0d30zSy.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2025-12-17\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:0;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:0;}i:10;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/zwzQEy8GM4GW3VG3FE9w0jBQeaX.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:1590839;s:5:\"title\";s:39:\"Edward Abbey, naturellement subversif !\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"fr\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:39:\"Edward Abbey, naturellement subversif !\";s:8:\"overview\";s:356:\"A resistance writer and pioneer of nature writing with a controversial personality, Edward Abbey wrote more than twenty books on the theme of eternal nature. A gem of counterculture, his 1975 novel The Monkey Wrench Gang inspired a generation of environmental activists and readers with rebellious souls. Portrait of a rebellious, lyrical, and rude writer.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.421;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/oQf55ATXbwl3b0VAPgwydsgPbKv.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2025-11-14\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:6;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:1;}i:11;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/vWzyi3oVz3Pc6p8SIGtRS9CwJOY.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:2:{i:0;i:12;i:1;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:410158;s:5:\"title\";s:8:\"Atlantic\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:8:\"Atlantic\";s:8:\"overview\";s:184:\"Documentary about the two big resources in the North Atlantic, fish and oil, and the impact of their exploitation on the environment in various countries on both sides of the Atlantic.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.353;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/6IVotlM1uEvgmSMX8HHdi3qpn36.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2016-02-05\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:7;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:0;}i:12;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/kG9fn7QfjgtPnCKeI3ygxPvFaOz.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:532558;s:5:\"title\";s:9:\"Albatross\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:9:\"Albatross\";s:8:\"overview\";s:142:\"A powerful visual journey into the heart of a gut-wrenching environmental tragedy, while delivering a profound message of healing and renewal.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.2181;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/fmCy1PDXsafbYv9jcoziwRBWb1t.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2013-01-01\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:10;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:2;}i:13;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";N;s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:239472;s:5:\"title\";s:26:\"Mysteries of the Driftless\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:26:\"Mysteries of the Driftless\";s:8:\"overview\";s:728:\"What strange forces saved one isolated section along the Upper Mississippi River from the repeated crushing and scouring effects of glaciers during the last two million years? And what pre-Ice Age throwbacks survived here in this unique geologic refuge that holds more Native American effigy mounds, petroglyph caves, strange geological features, and rare species than anywhere in the Midwest? These questions and more are answered in this captivating new documentary. A team of scientists embarks on a journey of exploration to expose both the science and threats behind three unique features of the zone - rare plants and animals, odd geological phenomenon, and striking remnants of a Native American pilgrimage like no other.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.031;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/sPB8JhHh1hT3yY3GZBTOAAWtmp8.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2013-09-16\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:0;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:0;}i:14;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/vaNkSQJes5wjad45Dyy1MlE7r8G.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:2:{i:0;i:10402;i:1;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:819702;s:5:\"title\";s:11:\"Hidden Eden\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:11:\"Hidden Eden\";s:8:\"overview\";s:995:\"Exploring the concept of the Ecology of Emotions, this musical film portrays an inner journey through the secret garden of creativity put into frame by the nature of Iceland. Hidden Eden is a metaphor for our inner secret garden of creativity. This project bloomed during an art residency in Iceland, sparked by conversations around our shared philosophies on voice and emotional connection. The nature of Iceland inspired us to make the connection on how the landscape reflects the emotional states of creativity and how it helps manage the homeostasis of our inner emotional landscapes. This exchange between emotion and the landscape opens a space for healing. Creativity provides us with the tools to access a garden of our authentic being, nourishing and balancing us. Allowing ourselves to explore the spectrum of our emotions through the lens of our relationship with the Earth invites others to do the same. The creative process can affect our well being and is a key to human evolution.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:0.9617;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/olPlJN91fbdJ6YRny1CAP36RioE.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2021-03-19\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:10;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:1;}i:15;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";N;s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:1673177;s:5:\"title\";s:14:\"Saving Spoonie\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"de\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:14:\"Saving Spoonie\";s:8:\"overview\";s:721:\"Spoonie, the spoon-billed sandpiper, would have long since gone extinct without Dr. Christoph Zöckler and a tight-knit group of international ornithologists. As if that weren’t bad enough, the migration route of this sparrow-sized wading bird—with its peculiar spoon-shaped bill—runs from Russia through North Korea and China all the way to Myanmar, passing through several of the world’s crisis regions of the past decade. The work of the task force is therefore also a political challenge. It requires diplomatic sensitivity in coordinating with the countries along the flyway. In the tragicomic story of Spoonie’s fate, the struggle for threatened biodiversity in an increasingly fragile world is reflected.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.1092;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/azceQL5rxWLpxMOMgx98JCZsZSz.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2026-06-25\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:0;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:0;}i:16;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/sDVOwasmTiW7klK3gFwdSga49YC.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:1619019;s:5:\"title\";s:10:\"The Shrimp\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:10:\"The Shrimp\";s:8:\"overview\";s:301:\"The Shrimp is a lush visualist\'s documentary that follows the life cycle of a shrimp along the marshes of Savannah, Georgia. Beautifully etched images and a canny audio soundtrack create a rich observational work about Southern culture, human folly and the interplay of natural and built environments.\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:0.7729;s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/90r4WgiIjoqvcaSZCawpwjGyCTU.jpg\";s:12:\"release_date\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:7;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:1;}i:17;a:15:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/9trJj4yG18FGT29pPnUjtJd2ouq.jpg\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:99;}s:2:\"id\";i:432602;s:5:\"title\";s:38:\"An Inconvenient Sequel: Truth to Power\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:38:\"An Inconvenient Sequel: Truth to Power\";s:8:\"overview\";s:612:\"A decade after An Inconvenient Truth brought climate change into the heart of popular culture comes the riveting and rousing follow-up that shows just how close we are to a real energy revolution. Vice President Al Gore continues his tireless fight, traveling around the world training an army of climate champions and influencing international climate policy. Cameras follow him behind the scenes—in moments private and public, funny and poignant—as he pursues the empowering notion that while the stakes have never been higher, the perils of climate change can be overcome with human ingenuity and passion.\";s:10:\"popu