he land in danger, Poppy, Branch, and their band of friends must embark on an epic quest to create harmony among the feuding Trolls to unite them against certain doom.\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/7W0G3YECgDAfnuiHG91r8WqgIOe.jpg\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:5:\"movie\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:6:{i:0;i:10751;i:1;i:16;i:2;i:35;i:3;i:14;i:4;i:12;i:5;i:10402;}s:10:\"popularity\";d:7.4003;s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2020-03-11\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:7.235;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:2283;}i:7;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/kQ8XfGdLVXqWbd63L7lg6Dm7mby.jpg\";s:2:\"id\";i:44825;s:5:\"title\";s:8:\"Live Aid\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:8:\"Live Aid\";s:8:\"overview\";s:427:\"Live Aid was held on 13 July 1985, simultaneously in Wembley Stadium in London, England, and the John F. Kennedy Stadium in Philadelphia, United States. It was one of the largest scale satellite link-ups and television broadcasts of all time: watched live by an estimated global audience of 1.9 billion, across 150 nations. \"It\'s twelve noon in London, seven AM in Philadelphia, and around the world it\'s time for Live Aid...!\"\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/bK0KMcbe3LMIoCIBiIAlIRONJKL.jpg\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:5:\"movie\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:2:{i:0;i:10402;i:1;i:99;}s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.6994;s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"1985-07-13\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:7.9;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:52;}i:8;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/a5IKYyLryMcsRsjKJ0yePcadK8T.jpg\";s:2:\"id\";i:79931;s:5:\"title\";s:36:\"Adele: Live at the Royal Albert Hall\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:36:\"Adele: Live at the Royal Albert Hall\";s:8:\"overview\";s:159:\"On September 22nd 2011, Adele played The Royal Albert Hall in London. A dream come true moment and a highlight of her record breaking year with the album \'21\'.\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32