";i:0;}}}i:7;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/d0GhwTlOdLEkTad6DvxarlTb0rQ.jpg\";s:2:\"id\";i:103577;s:4:\"name\";s:22:\"Cartoon\'s Neighborhood\";s:13:\"original_name\";s:25:\"شعبية الكرتون\";s:8:\"overview\";s:126:\"A cartoon comedy TV series in the United Arab Emirates that revolves around social and cultural values in the Emirati society.\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/ly7Mndsxgm3NEkPdYGDkxGRiJAZ.jpg\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:2:\"tv\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"ar\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:4:{i:0;i:16;i:1;i:35;i:2;i:10751;i:3;i:10762;}s:10:\"popularity\";d:4.0573;s:14:\"first_air_date\";s:10:\"2006-09-23\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:7;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:5;s:14:\"origin_country\";a:1:{i:0;s:2:\"AE\";}}i:8;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/9f1oZlGyA4CLAf1qsQqOZhpO2k4.jpg\";s:2:\"id\";i:84795;s:4:\"name\";s:7:\"Cartoon\";s:13:\"original_name\";s:7:\"Cartoon\";s:8:\"overview\";s:161:\"Cartoonist Aritra’s life turns upside down when mysterious things start happening in his new apartment. Mayhem ensues when a paranormal activist dies suddenly.\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/20HS6QjZE1n0TCl8D5Z8GTOhXo4.jpg\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:2:\"tv\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"bn\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:0:{}s:10:\"popularity\";d:0.8518;s:14:\"first_air_date\";s:10:\"2017-09-26\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:0;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:0;s:14:\"origin_country\";a:1:{i:0;s:2:\"IN\";}}i:9;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";N;s:2:\"id\";i:2166;s:4:\"name\";s:14:\"Cartoon Planet\";s:13:\"original_name\";s:14:\"Cartoon Planet\";s:8:\"overview\";s:867:\"Cartoon Planet is an animated variety show that originally ran from 1995 to 1998, and from March 30, 2012 to present on Cartoon Network. A spin-off of the animated Space Ghost Coast to Coast talk show, the original premise was that Space Ghost had recruited his imprisoned evil arch nemesis Zorak and his loud and extremely dimwitted archenemy Brak to assist him in hosting a variety show.\n\nCartoon Planet began as an hour-long block of cartoons hosted by Space Ghost, Zorak, and Brak. They would introduce full cartoons from the Turner Entertainment library, such as old theatrical shorts and Hanna-Barbera cartoons, including the original 1960s Space Ghost episodes. The host segments were often original songs and ad libbed skits. New material ceased being made in 1997, and most of the songs and skits were re-packaged into 22 half-hour episodes without cartoons.\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/pcRa0lqzDsbm8s5N0Nh2zDj0tTO.jpg\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:2:\"tv\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:3:{i:0;i:16;i:1;i:35;i:2;i:10762;}s:10:\"popularity\";d:2.1;s:14:\"first_air_date\";s:10:\"1995-09-10\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:8.4;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:5;s:14:\"origin_country\";a:1:{i:0;s:2:\"US\";}}i:10;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";N;s:2:\"id\";i:4818;s:4:\"name\";s:13:\"Cartoon Alley\";s:13:\"original_name\";s:13:\"Cartoon Alley\";s:8:\"overview\";s:1247:\"Cartoon Alley is an American television program that aired on Turner Classic Movies every Saturday Morning at 11:30 AM ET.\n\nHosted by Ben Mankiewicz, the series featured three classic animated shorts from the 1930-1950\'s per episode. Most shorts were from The Golden Age of American animation. Each of the three shorts focused on a common theme. Most shorts came from Warner Bros., MGM, and Paramount, but during the show\'s first season Cartoon Alley featured shorts from the Gaumont Film Company. Many recognizable characters have been featured in at least one episode such as Bugs Bunny, Popeye, Porky Pig, Tom and Jerry, and others not so famous such as Goopy Geer and The Captain and the Kids. The shorts often appeared uncut and uncensored, and the more controversial cartoons were often introduced with a brief warning by Mankiewicz about the ethnic stereotypes being portrayed. The network\'s logo was only featured for a brief time, usually during the last short featured.\n\nFrom November 2004 to September 2005 the series was featured just once a month but after popular demand the series became a weekly feature. This series never aired in February because of TCM\'s 31 Days of Oscars programming. The series was canceled in autumn of 2007.\";s:11:\"poster_path\";N;s:10:\"media_type\";s:2:\"tv\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:16;}s:10:\"popularity\";d:3.4372;s:14:\"first_air_date\";s:10:\"2004-11-05\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:8;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:1;s:14:\"origin_country\";a:1:{i:0;s:2:\"US\";}}i:11;a:10:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:2:\"id\";i:3099508;s:4:\"name\";s:14:\"Cartoon Natcha\";s:13:\"original_name\";s:14:\"Cartoon Natcha\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:6:\"person\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:0;s:6:\"gender\";i:0;s:20:\"known_for_department\";s:6:\"Acting\";s:12:\"profile_path\";N;s:9:\"known_for\";a:0:{}}i:12;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";N;s:2:\"id\";i:768558;s:5:\"title\";s:10:\"Cartoon 14\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:10:\"Cartoon 14\";s:8:\"overview\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/xyCP32LMOmjCz5lodoxezrQqBS3.jpg\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:5:\"movie\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"fr\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:16;}s:10:\"popularity\";d:0.58;s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"1988-03-11\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:7;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:1;}i:13;a:10:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:2:\"id\";i:5379408;s:4:\"name\";s:17:\"Cartoon Bondurant\";s:13:\"original_name\";s:17:\"Cartoon Bondurant\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:6:\"person\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:0;s:6:\"gender\";i:0;s:20:\"known_for_department\";s:6:\"Acting\";s:12:\"profile_path\";N;s:9:\"known_for\";a:1:{i:0;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/8JNiP6RYiu0ROmykpojRLCHJZGl.jpg\";s:2:\"id\";i:1466299;s:5:\"title\";s:12:\"Marijuambies\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:12:\"Marijuambies\";s:8:\"overview\";s:552:\"\"Marijuambies\" is a hilarious new comedy that follows the story of a weed dealer and his hippie friend who accidentally sell poisoned weed, turning their customers into zombies. As the duo realizes the dangerous effects of their tainted product, they embark on a wild journey to find a cure and stop the zombie apocalypse they inadvertently caused. Along the way, they encounter various challenges and eccentric characters, leading to a series of mishaps and adventures that will keep audiences laughing from start to finish.  Directed by Brian Foster.\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/t8kKdKBILYbEtPiNTOREDJ6lAFO.jpg\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:5:\"movie\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:35;}s:10:\"popularity\";d:0.1186;s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2025-04-20\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:5.5;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:2;}}}i:14;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";N;s:2:\"id\";i:1190042;s:5:\"title\";s:7:\"Cartoon\";s:14:\"original_title\";s:7:\"Cartoon\";s:8:\"overview\";s:31:\"One of Ken Jacobs\' Eternalisms.\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/lTuehH1hXSnEo6PZtjgHfUGNq3m.jpg\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:5:\"movie\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:0:{}s:10:\"popularity\";d:0.0286;s:12:\"release_date\";s:10:\"2019-01-01\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:5:\"video\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:0;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:0;}i:15;a:10:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:2:\"id\";i:4511180;s:4:\"name\";s:23:\"Cartoon Gingkan Boonsuk\";s:13:\"original_name\";s:23:\"Cartoon Gingkan Boonsuk\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:6:\"person\";s:10:\"popularity\";d:0.1304;s:6:\"gender\";i:0;s:20:\"known_for_department\";s:6:\"Acting\";s:12:\"profile_path\";N;s:9:\"known_for\";a:3:{i:0;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";N;s:2:\"id\";i:50439;s:4:\"name\";s:12:\"Noose of Sin\";s:13:\"original_name\";s:21:\"บ่วงบาป\";s:8:\"overview\";s:401:\"Bangkok Rattanakosin era, 116, or about the year 1898 during the reign of the fifth Lord Suradej (Ayothaya) gave landholders and property everything, including an attendant slave to his only son is Khunphithak. Lady Jewell, his wife, filled with anxiety knowing that fact Khunphithak son is not robust. They live happy life from day to day, but the last in the frame for fear of his father\'s prestige.\";s:11:\"poster_path\";N;s:10:\"media_type\";s:2:\"tv\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"en\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:2:{i:0;i:18;i:1;i:10766;}s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.4481;s:14:\"first_air_date\";s:10:\"2013-02-07\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:6;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:2;s:14:\"origin_country\";a:1:{i:0;s:2:\"TH\";}}i:1;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";s:32:\"/fwJIQh3NeNufWOnbig4EKdAARuZ.jpg\";s:2:\"id\";i:261264;s:4:\"name\";s:5:\"Gomin\";s:13:\"original_name\";s:24:\"โกมินทร์\";s:8:\"overview\";s:497:\"In Gusinakhon, there was a king named Gosutum. He had three sons: the eldest was named Gomes, the second Gomon and the youngest brother, which was powerful because he was born with a special item with him, was Gomin.\n\nThe little prince, with only 12 years old, had dexterity and individuality with magic weapons causing Gomin to not be afraid of anyone. One day, Gomin and his friend Musa went to the beach and met with the son of Kato Naga, the royal city of the underworld, and Gomin killed him.\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/1ipEf7mG3Z5CUAWCMllhiV7j6e4.jpg\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:2:\"tv\";s:17:\"original_language\";s:2:\"th\";s:9:\"genre_ids\";a:1:{i:0;i:18;}s:10:\"popularity\";d:1.3816;s:14:\"first_air_date\";s:10:\"2004-12-31\";s:8:\"softcore\";b:0;s:12:\"vote_average\";d:0;s:10:\"vote_count\";i:0;s:14:\"origin_country\";a:1:{i:0;s:2:\"TH\";}}i:2;a:16:{s:5:\"adult\";b:0;s:13:\"backdrop_path\";N;s:2:\"id\";i:261293;s:4:\"name\";s:25:\"This Person is our Father\";s:13:\"original_name\";s:45:\"คนนี้แหละพ่อเรา\";s:8:\"overview\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"poster_path\";s:32:\"/g0CT6MbC77Bg3SGic2Wy3JYrFDb.jpg\";s:10:\"media_type\";s:2:\"tv\";s:17:\"origi